# Controls what `gcloud builds submit` uploads as source to Cloud Build. WITHOUT this
# file present, gcloud silently falls back to .gitignore's rules applied straight to the
# filesystem — and .gitignore has a blanket `checkpoints/` rule (it normally keeps large
# model weights out of git; the ones that ARE committed here were force-added with
# `git add -f`, which gcloud has no way to know about). That fallback stripped
# modeling/checkpoints/qwen3vl-lora-final2/ out of the uploaded tarball entirely, so
# vlm_service/Dockerfile's `COPY modeling/checkpoints/qwen3vl-lora-final2 ...` failed
# with "file not found in build context" even though the file is right there on disk and
# in git. This file's presence makes gcloud use ONLY these rules, not .gitignore's.
#
# Mirrors .dockerignore's intent (same files vlm_service/Dockerfile actually needs from
# a repo-root build context) but does NOT exclude the checkpoint directory.
.git/
.claude/

frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
backend/.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

guard/

modeling/outputs/
modeling/notebooks/
modeling/checkpoints/blip2-lora-final/
modeling/dataset/
mlruns/

docs/
*.md
!vlm_service/README.md
